@startuml nl2sql_dagents_integration
title NL2SQL demo integration with the Dagents framework

left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #F7F3EA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Aptos"
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam ArrowColor #53635B
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Presenter / user" as User

package "services/nl2sql-demo" as App #FFFFFF {
  rectangle "React frontend\nsample prompt, schema JSON,\nDagents trace" as UI #E8EFF6
  rectangle "FastAPI backend\nPOST /api/v1/generate" as API #E3EEE6
  rectangle "DagentsOrchestrator\nfunctional_trace(...)" as Orchestrator #F0E2C8
  rectangle "NL2SQLModelRegistry\nCodeT5 / CodeQwen / fallback" as Registry #F3DCD3
}

package "Dagents framework" as Dagents #EFE4CE {
  rectangle "agents.common.infrastructure\ndagents_runner" as Runner #E9E1FA
  rectangle "dagentsc\nOCaml planner CLI" as DCLI #E9E1FA
  package "HTTP services called by the app" as HttpServices {
    rectangle "core-service\n/workloads:compile\n/services /topology" as Core #F4E8D0
    rectangle "pipeline-service\n/pipelines\n/pipelines/{id}/runs" as Pipeline #F4E8D0
    rectangle "model-service\n/datasets\n/model-jobs" as Model #F4E8D0
    rectangle "LMA\n/datasets:profile" as LMA #DCEBE1
    rectangle "GMA\n/datasets:profile" as GMA #DCE7F1
  }
}

User --> UI : asks a question
UI --> API : question + schema tables
API --> Orchestrator : build Dagents trace
API --> Registry : generate SQL

Orchestrator --> Runner : source validation,\nextraction planning,\nschema checks,\nquality rules
Runner --> DCLI : JSON request
DCLI --> Runner : JSON plan/report

Orchestrator --> Core : catalog, topology,\ncompile NL2SQL workload
Orchestrator --> Pipeline : register and run\nschema workflow
Orchestrator --> Model : list model datasets/jobs
Orchestrator --> LMA : source schema profile
Orchestrator --> GMA : assimilated schema profile

Registry --> API : SQL + prompt + fallback flag
Orchestrator --> API : trace steps and payloads
API --> UI : generated SQL + DDL + trace

note bottom of DCLI
  The OCaml layer is called at request time
  for validation and planning. It is also
  built into containers before runtime.
end note
@enduml
